  "specialRules": [
    "All British, Portuguese and Brunswick infantry: Steady Line, First Fire, Cannot Form Attack Column, Mixed Formation, Must Form Square, and can form skirmish order in terrain they couldn't normally enter.",
    "Skirmish: only the Riflemen, Light infantry and Caçadores can adopt skirmish formation; other troops only to enter terrain they couldn't otherwise, or as part of a mixed formation.",
    "Gallop at Anything: +1 to Charge orders and Ferocious Charge, but the unit must make a breakthrough move if allowed, even off the table; British cavalry suffer +2 to their Command roll when they leave the table like this.",
    "Heavy Cavalry D1: Dragoons add one to any combat result, rather than between one and three.",
    "Shrapnel: British guns can fire at medium range with 3 dice, but need 5s to hit."
  ]
}
